    "body": "Hi there! \n\nI'm looking into adding a romanization step to [Storyteller's](https://storyteller-platform.gitlab.io/storyteller) alignment algorithm as part of supporting more languages. This library seems like it does almost everything we need!\n\nOne thing that I think we'll need that doesn't seem to exist yet here is a position mapping. Ideally it would be possible, while generating the transliteration, to produce a mapping that allows you to convert a position in the transliterated string to one in the original string (and vice versa).\n\nThis is important for Storyteller, because we'll be doing a fuzzy search on the transliterated text, but we then need to be able to look up the start and end times for the match, which will be based on the original text.\n\nIf this is something that you're open to, I would be happy to contribute it when it comes time for me to start working on this. I imagine it would be optional, either a new set of functions (`transliterateWithMapping`, `slugifyWithMapping`, bad names but you get the picture) or a new option to the existing functions. When passed, the functions will return both the result string and some mapping object. \n\nI think it would make sense to model the mapping on [prosemirror-transform's Mapping interface](https://github.com/ProseMirror/prosemirror-transform/blob/master/src/map.ts), which is an efficient way of implementing exactly what we need. ",
