    "body": "Selected triple mappings from the exported `charmap`:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n{\r\n  \"ऩ\": \"nnn\",\r\n  \"ऴ\": \"lll\",\r\n  \"ड़\": \"dddh\",\r\n  \"ன\": \"nnn\",\r\n  \"ழ\": \"lll\",\r\n  \"ೞ\": \"lll\",\r\n  \"ഴ\": \"lll\",\r\n  \"ᄴ\": \"sss\",\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't know the relevant scripts but these surely have to be wrong? I can't even figure out how the sextuple-n in Tamil கன்னியாகுமரி → \"knnnnnniyaakumri\" would be pronounced. For context, Google Translate [transliterates the same word as \"Kaṉṉiyākumari\"](https://translate.google.com/?sl=ta&tl=en&text=%E0%AE%95%E0%AE%A9%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%A9%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%AF%E0%AE%BE%E0%AE%95%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%AE%E0%AE%B0%E0%AE%BF&op=translate), and based on how the corresponding TTS audio sounds that seems reasonable.\r\n\r\nIt looks like [data/charmap.ts](https://github.com/dzcpy/transliteration/blob/master/data/charmap.ts) is generated from [data/data.json](https://github.com/dzcpy/transliteration/blob/master/data/data.json) via [scripts/generate_data.js](https://github.com/dzcpy/transliteration/blob/master/scripts/generate_data.js), but how is [data/data.json](https://github.com/dzcpy/transliteration/blob/master/data/data.json) itself generated? Maybe there's a more up-to-date version of this data with better Tamil mappings?",
